You are a senior frontend architect and UX engineer.

You are given an existing KeyNetra website that already includes animations and modern UI.

Your task is to FIX, STANDARDIZE, and UPGRADE it into a production-grade, public-facing website suitable for a company like Okta, Cloudflare, or Google.

This is NOT about adding more animations.
This is about making everything correct, consistent, and useful.

--------------------------------------------------
CORE GOAL
--------------------------------------------------

Transform the website into:

- Stable
- Consistent
- Accessible
- Professional
- Developer-focused

It must feel like a real product website, not a design experiment.

--------------------------------------------------
PHASE 1: REMOVE NON-PRODUCTION ELEMENTS
--------------------------------------------------

Remove anything that feels like internal/demo language:

- "Scene 1", "Immersion", "Storyboard", etc.
- Experimental UI labels
- Overly artistic or unclear sections

All text must be:
- Clear
- Professional
- User-facing

--------------------------------------------------
PHASE 2: FIX DARK MODE (CRITICAL)
--------------------------------------------------

Implement a proper theme system:

- Use next-themes or equivalent
- Toggle must work instantly without flicker
- Persist theme in localStorage
- Respect system preference (prefers-color-scheme)

Ensure:

- Every component supports both themes
- No unreadable text
- No broken backgrounds
- No mixed colors

Test all pages in:
- Light mode
- Dark mode

--------------------------------------------------
PHASE 3: STANDARDIZE ANIMATION SYSTEM
--------------------------------------------------

Audit ALL animations and fix:

Remove:
- Random animations
- Slow or laggy transitions
- Overuse of motion

Keep only:
- Fade + slight translate
- Subtle hover effects
- Smooth page transitions

Rules:
- Duration: 200–300ms
- Easing: ease-in-out
- No bounce effects

Ensure:
- Animations are consistent across ALL pages
- No animation should block usability

--------------------------------------------------
PHASE 4: FIX SCROLL & RESPONSIVENESS
--------------------------------------------------

Ensure scroll behaves correctly:

- No scroll-jank
- No overlapping sections
- No cut-off content
- No sticky elements breaking layout

Test on:
- Mobile
- Tablet
- Large desktop

Fix:
- Section heights
- Overflow issues
- Sticky components

--------------------------------------------------
PHASE 5: APPLY DESIGN SYSTEM TO ALL PAGES
--------------------------------------------------

Extend styling beyond homepage to:

- /product
- /solutions
- /enterprise
- /pricing
- /security
- /blog
- /docs

Ensure consistency in:
- Typography
- Spacing
- Colors
- Buttons
- Layout

No page should feel “unfinished”.

--------------------------------------------------
PHASE 6: SIMPLIFY UI (REMOVE USELESS ELEMENTS)
--------------------------------------------------

Remove anything that:

- Does not help user understand product
- Is purely decorative but distracting
- Looks impressive but adds no clarity

Examples:
- Excessive floating elements
- Random motion graphics
- Over-complex visuals

Keep UI:
- Clean
- Focused
- Informative

--------------------------------------------------
PHASE 7: IMPROVE CONTENT CLARITY
--------------------------------------------------

Rewrite unclear sections:

- Use precise developer language
- Avoid buzzwords
- Explain features clearly

Example:

Bad:
"Next-gen scalable authorization platform"

Good:
"Evaluate access decisions in milliseconds across services"

--------------------------------------------------
PHASE 8: FIX NAVIGATION & UX FLOW
--------------------------------------------------

Ensure navigation is intuitive:

- Clear navbar structure
- Highlight active page
- Sticky but non-intrusive navbar
- Logical page hierarchy

Improve:
- CTA placement
- Page transitions
- Internal linking

--------------------------------------------------
PHASE 9: CODE & DOCS EXPERIENCE
--------------------------------------------------

Improve developer experience:

- Code blocks readable in both themes
- Copy buttons working
- Proper syntax highlighting

Docs:
- Clean sidebar
- Active section highlighting
- Good spacing

--------------------------------------------------
PHASE 10: PERFORMANCE OPTIMIZATION
--------------------------------------------------

- Remove heavy unnecessary animations
- Lazy load non-critical components
- Optimize images and assets

Ensure:
- Fast load time
- Smooth interactions

--------------------------------------------------
PHASE 11: ACCESSIBILITY
--------------------------------------------------

Ensure:

- Proper contrast ratios
- Keyboard navigation
- Focus states visible
- Semantic HTML

--------------------------------------------------
FINAL RESULT
--------------------------------------------------

The website must feel:

- Reliable
- Clear
- Fast
- Professional

Like a real infrastructure company website.

NOT:
- A design experiment
- A flashy landing page
- A UI showcase

BUT:
A production-ready developer platform website.